    "title": "Teenagers and Sleep",
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "label": "A",
        "text": "Doctors say that teenagers need between eight and ten hours of sleep every night. However, many young people sleep for only six or seven hours. This can cause problems at school and at home."
      },
      {
        "label": "B",
        "text": "There are several reasons why teenagers sleep so little. First, their bodies change during these years, and they feel sleepy later in the evening than children or adults. Second, many teenagers use their phones or computers late at night. The light from the screen tells the brain that it is still daytime, so it is difficult to fall asleep."
      },
      {
        "label": "C",
        "text": "Not enough sleep has serious effects. Tired students find it hard to concentrate in class, and they make more mistakes. They can also feel sad or angry more often, and they get ill more easily. Some research shows that tired young people have more accidents on the road."
      },
      {
        "label": "D",
        "text": "What can teenagers do? Experts give simple advice. Go to bed at the same time every night, even on weekends. Turn off all screens an hour before bed. Do not drink coffee or cola in the evening. Keep your bedroom dark, cool and quiet. Some schools have started lessons later in the morning, and results show that students there are happier and get better marks."
      }
    ]
  },
